```

## How to compile:

Requires a C++23-capable compiler: GCC 13+ or Clang 16+ recommended.
Older toolchains such as GCC 8.x fail on `<ranges>` (C++20). The optional
stacktrace support (`-DCXX23`, on by default when `libstdc++exp` is found)
needs GCC 12.1+; disable it with `-DCXX23=OFF`.

```bash
mkdir build
cd build
cmake .. -DSTATIC=OFF
make -j$(nproc)
```

To cross compile, use something like (static compilation), considering that `mips-openwrt-linux-musl-gcc` is the gcc executable for that platform:

```bash
cmake -B build . -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=arm-linux-gnueabihf-g++ -DSTATIC=ON -DNETCVCLIENT=0
cd build
make -j$(nproc)
```

To compile using the Docker container (useful to cross compile):

```bash
docker run -it --rm -v ./workspace:/workspace catalinii/minisatip-build-image:latest

cd /workspace/
git clone https://github.com/catalinii/minisatip.git

cd minisatip/
cmake -B build . -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=mipsel-linux-gnu-g++ -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_TARGET=mipsel-linux-gnu -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DSTATIC=ON -DNETCVCLIENT=0 -DSRT=0 -DDVBCSA=0 -DDVBCA=0 -DDDCI=0
(cd build && make -j$(nproc))
mipsel-linux-gnu-strip build/minisatip
cp build/minisatip /workspace/minisatip.mips

cd /workspace/
rm -rf minisatip
```

